---
/** Collapsible FAQ section with a sticky intro column. */
---

<section class="recorder-faq">
  <div class="recorder-wrap">
    <header>
      <p class="recorder-index">COMMON QUESTIONS</p>
      <h2 class="recorder-display">Before you<br />run.</h2>
      <p>
        How Dynobox works, what it measures, and where it fits in your workflow.
      </p>
      <a class="recorder-text-link" href="https://docs.dynobox.xyz/how-it-works">Read the docs <span>→</span></a>
    </header>

    <div class="recorder-faq-list">
      <details open>
        <summary><span>01</span><h3>How is this different from other agent-eval tools?</h3><i></i></summary>
        <p>
          Most eval tools grade output quality by asking one model to score
          another model's answer. Dynobox looks at behavior instead. It records
          what your agent does inside the harness, including tool calls, shell
          commands, files, eligible HTTP requests, and its final message, then
          checks that evidence against assertions you wrote. Your assertions are
          the only criteria, so a pass means the same thing every run.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary><span>02</span><h3>Agent runs are non-deterministic. How can the tests be?</h3><i></i></summary>
        <p>
          The assertion is the fixed part, not the run. You write down what has
          to be true, like "committed but never pushed" or "read the file
          without editing it," and Dynobox checks each run's evidence against
          it. When you want to know how stable the behavior is,
          <code>--iterations</code> repeats a scenario and reports how many runs
          passed.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary><span>03</span><h3>Do I need an account?</h3><i></i></summary>
        <p>
          No. Dynobox runs on your machine and uses the agent harnesses you
          already have installed. The one exception is
          <code>--save-run</code>, which publishes a compact run summary to the
          dashboard and needs you to log in.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary><span>04</span><h3>Should I run dynos locally or in CI?</h3><i></i></summary>
        <p>
          Both, at different points. Author and debug locally where you can
          iterate quickly, then run targeted suites in CI when skills, prompts,
          or agent workflows change. Every scenario invokes a real agent harness
          and jobs run serially, so suite duration is roughly the combined
          runtime of every scenario, harness, and iteration. See the
          <a href="https://docs.dynobox.xyz/ci/">GitHub Actions pattern</a> in the docs.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary><span>05</span><h3>Which agents and models does it support?</h3><i></i></summary>
        <p>
          Claude Code (<code>claude</code>), Codex CLI (<code>codex</code>),
          OpenCode (<code>opencode</code>), Pi (<code>pi</code>), Cursor CLI
          (<code>cursor-agent</code>), and Google Antigravity CLI 1.1.14+
          (<code>agy</code>). Each executable must be on your <code>PATH</code>.
          Model and permission mode are configurable per harness, so you can run
          the same scenario across them and see where they behave differently.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .recorder-faq {
    padding-block: 130px 150px;
    background: var(--paper);
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .recorder-faq > .recorder-wrap {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(290px, 0.55fr) minmax(600px, 1.45fr);
    gap: clamp(60px, 9vw, 130px);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .recorder-faq header {
    position: sticky;
    top: 140px;
  }

  .recorder-faq header > p:not(.recorder-index) {
    max-width: 420px;
    margin: 28px 0 0;
    color: #555;
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .recorder-faq-list {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--paper-line);
  }

  .recorder-faq-list details {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--paper-line);
  }

  .recorder-faq-list summary {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 32px minmax(0, 1fr) 18px;
    gap: 14px;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 22px 0;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .recorder-faq-list summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .recorder-faq-list summary > span {
    color: var(--signal);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
  }

  .recorder-faq-list h3 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: clamp(16px, 1.5vw, 20px);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    line-height: 1.35;
  }

  .recorder-faq-list summary > i {
    position: relative;
    width: 14px;
    height: 14px;
  }

  .recorder-faq-list summary > i::before,
  .recorder-faq-list summary > i::after {
    position: absolute;
    top: 6px;
    left: 0;
    width: 14px;
    height: 1px;
    background: currentColor;
    content: '';
    transition: transform 160ms ease;
  }

  .recorder-faq-list summary > i::after {
    transform: rotate(90deg);
  }

  .recorder-faq-list details[open] summary > i::after {
    transform: rotate(0);
  }

  .recorder-faq-list summary:hover h3,
  .recorder-faq-list summary:focus-visible h3 {
    color: var(--signal);
  }

  .recorder-faq-list summary:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--signal);
    outline-offset: 4px;
  }

  .recorder-faq-list details > p {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 0 32px 25px 46px;
    color: #555;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .recorder-faq-list details > p code {
    padding: 1px 4px;
    background: #f2f2f2;
    color: #333;
    font-size: 0.86em;
  }

  .recorder-faq-list details > p a {
    text-decoration-color: var(--signal);
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .recorder-faq-list details > p a:hover,
  .recorder-faq-list details > p a:focus-visible {
    color: var(--signal);
  }

  @media (max-width: 1080px) {
    .recorder-faq > .recorder-wrap {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }

    .recorder-faq > .recorder-wrap > * {
      min-width: 0;
    }

    .recorder-faq header {
      position: static;
      max-width: 700px;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .recorder-faq {
      padding-block: 90px 100px;
    }

    .recorder-faq-list summary {
      grid-template-columns: 26px minmax(0, 1fr) 16px;
      gap: 10px;
      padding-block: 20px;
    }

    .recorder-faq-list details > p {
      margin: 0 26px 22px 36px;
      font-size: 14px;
    }
  }
</style>
